  <h2>Gender Disparity in Homicide Victimization</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">Gender is one of the most consistent and significant predictors of homicide victimization globally. Male victims vastly outnumber female victims in nearly every country and year in the dataset.</p>

  <p>Across 155 countries with matched male and female data, <strong>the median male-to-female homicide rate ratio is 3.35</strong>: men die from homicide at more than three times the rate of women. The mean ratio is even higher (though skewed by extreme outliers). This disparity has been consistent throughout the 1990–2023 period.</p>

